      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, you cannot reliably determine if pandas returns a view or a copy using built-in properties at runtime because the behavior depends heavily on your data alignment and version. If you are certain you do not want a copy, you can wrap your operation in `np.copy()` or use `pd.concat()` on the regions. To finalize your main dataset, the safer bet is to explicitly create a view (e.g., `df.loc[...]=val`), or better yet, always modify the original dataframe directly through indexing rather than filtering midway through the workflow.",
      "source": "target",
